    "result_text": "Green. I agreed with both findings and addressed them.\n\n**Both findings were valid \u2014 fixed.**\n\n1. **Business logic moved to a model class.** The date arithmetic + multi-threshold classification is substantive derivation, matching the shape of `CityRegions.identityRegion` / `LuhnCheckDigit.of` / `OwnerIdentity.of`. I extracted it to a new `model/AgeBand` enum with a static `AgeBand.of(birthDate, referenceDate)` that lives beside `Owner` (same package as its neighbours, so no package cycle) and carries the Javadoc for the rule. `OwnerMapper.toAgeBand` is now a trivial delegate \u2014 it calls `AgeBand.of(...)` and bridges the domain enum to `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum` by name, so only the trivial DTO-wrapping stays inline (like `toContactPreference`).\n\n2. **Fully-qualified names removed.** With the logic relocated, `LocalDate`/`Period` are now top-of-file imports in `AgeBand`, and the mapper no longer references either type inline. I added the `AgeBand` import alongside `CityRegions` in the mapper, matching the file's import style.\n\nAcceptance behaviour is unchanged (`AgeBand.of` uses the identical thresholds and `Period.between` computation), and the test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).",
